meta {
  name: GetResource — the credential does not come back
  type: grpc
  seq: 3
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.ResourceService/GetResource
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "id": "{{integrationId}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5).

  It is worth running this request right after `SetCredential`: the response
  carries `credential_ref` — an opaque label derivable from the row itself — and
  **never** the secret. There is no path to read the value through the API;
  whoever needs it is the executor, straight from the vault (ADR-0001).
}
